1. Mathematical Preliminaries

We recall the essential formal structures used throughout the ULM construction.

1.1 Fractal Geometry and Iterated Function Systems

Definition 1 (Iterated Function System).
Let (X,d) be a complete metric space. A family of contractions \{\phi_i\}_{i=1}^N, \phi_i:X\to X with contraction ratios r_i\in(0,1), is called an iterated function system (IFS). The attractor F\subset X is the unique non‑empty compact set satisfying

F = \bigcup_{i=1}^N \phi_i(F).

Definition 2 (Similarity Dimension).
If all \phi_i are similitudes, the similarity dimension s is the unique solution of

\sum_{i=1}^N r_i^s = 1.

Theorem 1 (Moran–Hutchinson, 1981).
If the IFS satisfies the Open Set Condition (OSC) — there exists a non‑empty bounded open set V such that \phi_i(V)\subset V and \phi_i(V)\cap\phi_j(V)=\emptyset for i\neq j — then the Hausdorff dimension \dim_H(F) equals the similarity dimension s.

Proof. See Hutchinson (1981), Falconer (2003). ∎

1.2 Information Thermodynamics

Landauer’s Principle: Erasing one bit of information in a physical system at temperature T dissipates at least k_B T \ln 2 joules, where k_B is Boltzmann’s constant.
Modern formulations (Bennett, 1982; Sagawa & Ueda, 2009) show that the bound is proportional to the algorithmic (Kolmogorov) complexity of the erased string when compression is allowed.

Derivation Entropy (Xu & Li, 2025).
Let a system be described by ontological states \mathcal{O} and carrier states \mathcal{C}. A derivation map f:\mathcal{C}\to\mathcal{O} computes the target state with a computational complexity \kappa(f). The derivation entropy is

S_{\mathrm{der}} = \min_{f} \left( S_{\mathrm{Shannon}}(\mathcal{C}) + \beta \, \kappa(f) \right),
\]  

where \beta couples physical energy to computation cost. The balance leads to a phase transition between memory‑dominant and computation‑dominant regimes. For the ULM, we adopt the simplified cost metric: the irreversible information processed by a capsule \kappa per forward pass, I(\kappa), multiplied by the Landauer factor.

1.3 Integrated Information Theory (IIT 4.0)

We follow the system integrated information formalism of Marshall et al. (2022). Consider a discrete dynamical system of n binary nodes with state X^t = (x_1^t,\dots,x_n^t) and transition probability matrix P(X^{t+1}\mid X^t).

Definition 3 (System Integrated Information \varphi_s).
Let \pi be a partition of the system into k independent parts. The partitioned transition matrix P^\pi is the product of the marginal transition matrices of each part. Then

\varphi_s = \min_{\pi} D\!\left(P \,\|\, P^\pi\right),
\]  

where D is the intrinsic difference (a generalisation of the Kullback–Leibler divergence respecting the state‑dependent cause‑effect structure). \varphi_s quantifies how much more information the whole generates than the sum of its parts.

For local causal mechanisms (individual capsules), we define the mechanism integrated information \varphi(m) as the \varphi_s value of the smallest complex containing m as an irreducible component. A standard approximation for Markovian systems is to take D(P\|P^\pi) as the KL divergence over the stationary distribution. We shall use this when operationalising the Φ‑threshold gate.

1.4 Category Theory Essentials

A category \mathcal{C} consists of a collection of objects \mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal{C}) and for each pair A,B a set of morphisms \mathrm{Hom}_{\mathcal{C}}(A,B), equipped with composition and identity morphisms satisfying associativity and unit laws.
A functor F:\mathcal{C}\to\mathcal{D} maps objects and morphisms preserving composition.
A pushout of a span A \xleftarrow{f} C \xrightarrow{g} B is an object P with morphisms A\to P, B\to P making the square commute and universal among such objects.

Polynomial endofunctor on \mathbf{Set}: F(X) = \sum_{b\in B} X^{E(b)}, where B is a set of "shapes" and E(b) a set of "positions". The initial algebra for F is the set of well‑founded trees; this captures recursive self‑similarity.

2. Formal Definition of the Universal Logic Matrix (ULM)

We construct the ULM as a category \mathcal{U} enriched with additional structure.

Definition 4 (Capsule).
A capsule \kappa is a tuple

\kappa = (S_\kappa, \Phi_\kappa, \Sigma_\kappa, E_\kappa),
\]  

where

· S_\kappa is a finite‑dimensional real vector space (the internal state space),
· \Phi_\kappa : S_\kappa \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} is the activation energy function,
· \Sigma_\kappa is an element of a signature space \mathcal{S} (e.g., a hash of its logical axioms),
· E_\kappa is a local energy budget (in joules).

The signature space \mathcal{S} is a metric space equipped with a distance d_{\mathcal{S}}.

Definition 5 (ULM Category).
The category \mathcal{U} has as objects all capsules \kappa. For capsules \kappa, \kappa', a morphism f: \kappa \to \kappa' is a linear map f: S_\kappa \to S_{\kappa'} together with a non‑negative weight w_f \in \mathbb{R}_+ representing the communication channel’s conductance. Composition is the usual composition of linear maps with multiplied weights.

We further equip \mathcal{U} with:

· A global energy functional \mathcal{E}: \mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal{U})\to\mathbb{R} (see Section 4).
· A causal graph G = (V,E) where V=\mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal{U}) and directed edges correspond to morphisms with w_f > \theta.
· A sheaf structure on G (Section 6).

Definition 6 (ULM Tuple, Revised).

\mathrm{ULM} = \langle \mathcal{U}, \Omega, \Sigma, \Delta, \Phi_{\min} \rangle,
\]  

where

· \mathcal{U} is the category of capsules,
· \Omega: \bigcup_{\kappa} S_\kappa \to \{\text{active},\text{dormant},\text{mutating}\} is the activation status function,
· \Sigma is the signature assignment \kappa\mapsto\Sigma_\kappa,
· \Delta is the collection of all morphisms (communication channels),
· \Phi_{\min}\in\mathbb{R}_+ is the global integration threshold.

3. Fractal Capsule Expansion and Hausdorff Dimension

We model the spawning of sub‑capsules as an IFS on a suitable space of capsule configurations.

Definition 7 (Configuration Space).
Let \mathcal{C} be the set of all finite multisets of capsules. We define a metric on \mathcal{C} using the Hausdorff distance on the signatures:

d(\{\kappa_i\}, \{\kappa'_j\}) = \max\Bigl\{ \sup_i \inf_j d_{\mathcal{S}}(\Sigma_{\kappa_i},\Sigma_{\kappa'_j}),\; \sup_j \inf_i d_{\mathcal{S}}(\Sigma_{\kappa'_j},\Sigma_{\kappa_i}) \Bigr\}.
\]  

Then (\mathcal{C}, d) is a complete metric space.

Definition 8 (Spawning IFS).
For each capsule \kappa, we define a spawning operation \phi_\kappa: \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C} as follows: given a configuration X\in\mathcal{C}, \phi_\kappa(X) replaces \kappa by a configuration consisting of \kappa together with n_\kappa identical copies of \kappa scaled in state space by a factor r_\kappa \in (0,1). More precisely, if \kappa is not present in X, \phi_\kappa(X)=X; if present, \phi_\kappa(X) is the multiset where one occurrence of \kappa is expanded into a cluster \{\kappa, \kappa^{(1)},\dots,\kappa^{(n_\kappa)}\}, each \kappa^{(i)} having state space r_\kappa S_\kappa and signature \Sigma_{\kappa^{(i)}} = h(\Sigma_\kappa) for a fixed contraction h:\mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{S}. The maps \phi_\kappa are chosen such that they are contractions on (\mathcal{C}, d) with ratios r_\kappa.

Lemma 1. The set \{\phi_\kappa\}_{\kappa\in K} for a finite indexing set K forms an IFS on \mathcal{C} with contraction ratios \{r_\kappa\}. If the spawning operations produce disjoint signature clusters (i.e., d_{\mathcal{S}}(h(\Sigma_\kappa), h(\Sigma_{\kappa'})) > 0 for distinct capsule lines), then the OSC holds for the open set V consisting of all configurations where any two signatures are separated by at least \delta.

Proof. (Sketch) Choose \delta smaller than the minimal distance between any two contracted signatures. The disjointness of the images of V under different \phi_\kappa follows from the separation of signatures, and \phi_\kappa(V)\subset V because the contraction reduces all distances uniformly. ∎

Theorem 2 (Fractal Dimension of ULM Expansion).
Let the ULM implement a spawning rule with a finite family of capsule types K and contraction ratios r_\kappa, satisfying the OSC. Then the attractor F of the IFS \{\phi_\kappa\}_{\kappa\in K} has Hausdorff dimension s given by the unique solution of

\sum_{\kappa\in K} r_\kappa^{s} = 1.
\]  

In particular, if all capsules spawn n offspring with identical ratio r, then

\dim_H(F) = \frac{\log n}{-\log r}.

Proof. By Lemma 1, the OSC is satisfied. By Theorem 1 (Moran–Hutchinson), the Hausdorff dimension equals the similarity dimension, which solves the stated equation. ∎

Thus the ULM’s recursive capsule expansion yields a genuine fractal with a computable Hausdorff dimension, rigorously linking architectural self‑similarity to metric geometry.

4. Thermodynamic Cost and Derivation Entropy

Definition 9 (Irreversible Information Cost).
For a capsule \kappa performing a computation (forward pass), let b(\kappa) be the number of bits of information that are erased (i.e., irreversibly overwritten). The minimal thermodynamic cost per activation is

C(\kappa) = k_B T \ln 2 \cdot b(\kappa) \quad \text{(joules)}.
\]  

If the computation can be made logically reversible, b(\kappa) can be reduced to the number of bits that are truly discarded.

Definition 10 (Derivation Entropy of a Capsule Cluster).
Given a set of capsules \mathcal{K} computing a joint output from an input, the derivation entropy is the minimal sum of Landauer costs over all paths in the causal graph, subject to the computational complexity of the mapping. Formally, let P be the set of all computational paths from input to output. For each path p, let B(p) be the total bits erased along p. Then

S_{\text{der}}(\mathcal{K}) = \min_{p\in P} k_B T \ln 2 \cdot B(p).
\]  

The global energy budget is E_{\text{total}} = \sum_{\kappa} E_\kappa. The system operates under the constraint S_{\text{der}}(\mathcal{K}) \le E_{\text{total}} for every task cycle.

Proposition 1 (Entropy–Energy Conservation).
The total energy consumed by the ULM over a time interval \Delta t satisfies

\Delta E_{\text{consumed}} \ge \Delta (S_{\text{der}}) + \Delta W_{\text{useful}},
\]  

where W_{\text{useful}} is any work done on the environment. In the ideal reversible limit equality holds.

Proof. Follows from the generalised Landauer principle (Sagawa & Ueda, 2009) applied to the total system plus environment. ∎

Thus the ULM’s capsule activation is governed by a precise, physically grounded cost function, and the “entropic budget” constraint of the original draft is now a derived thermodynamic bound.

5. Integrated Information Gate

We operationalise the \Phi-threshold gate using the local mechanism integrated information \varphi(m).

Definition 11 (Local \varphi for a Capsule).
Let \kappa be a capsule and let N(\kappa) be the set of capsules directly connected to \kappa via \Delta-morphisms (its neighbourhood). Consider the joint Markovian system consisting of \kappa and N(\kappa). Define the partition \pi that isolates \kappa as a separate mechanism. The mechanism integrated information \varphi(\kappa) is

\varphi(\kappa) = \min_{\pi} D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(P_{\kappa \cup N} \,\|\, P_{\kappa \cup N}^{\pi}\right),
\]  

where the KL divergence is evaluated at the stationary distribution of the full system. (Other divergence measures from IIT 4.0 may be substituted.)

Definition 12 (Activation Gate).
The status function \Omega maps capsule \kappa to active if and only if

\varphi(\kappa) \ge \Phi_{\min} \quad\text{and}\quad C(\kappa) \le E_\kappa.
\]  

Otherwise, it is dormant if C(\kappa) > E_\kappa but \varphi(\kappa) \ge \Phi_{\min}, and mutating if \varphi(\kappa) < \Phi_{\min}.

This makes the harmonic compatibility condition a precise computational threshold. The “Φ‑contribution” ambiguity is resolved by using the local mechanism \varphi, a well‑defined quantity per capsule.

Remark on Computability: The exact computation of \varphi(\kappa) is #P‑hard for general networks. For the ULM, we restrict to small neighbourhoods (e.g., up to 10 capsules) where exact methods or efficient approximations (Toker & Sommer, 2022) can be applied in real time.

6. Self‑Healing via Categorical Pushouts

The self‑healing mechanism is formalised as a pushout in the category \mathcal{U}.

Definition 13 (Fault Configuration).
A fault is a capsule \kappa_f whose \varphi(\kappa_f) drops below \Phi_{\min} persistently. The system has a backup capsule \kappa_b with the same signature \Sigma_{\kappa_b} = \Sigma_{\kappa_f} and identical state space but initially dormant.

Lemma 2 (Pushout Replacement).
Consider the span in \mathcal{U}:

\kappa_f \xleftarrow{\mathrm{id}} \kappa_f \xrightarrow{copy} \kappa_b,
\]  

where copy is the linear isomorphism mapping the current state of \kappa_f onto \kappa_b. Let the “context” be the sub‑ULM \mathcal{C} containing all other capsules and their connections to \kappa_f. The pushout of the span

\mathcal{C} \xleftarrow{\text{inclusion of }\kappa_f} \{\kappa_f\} \xrightarrow{copy} \{\kappa_b\}
\]  

in the category of ULM subcategories yields a new ULM where \kappa_b replaces \kappa_f while preserving all connections (morphisms) to the rest of the network.

Proof. The pushout of sets of capsules along the identity/copy maps is the disjoint union with \kappa_f identified with \kappa_b along the copy map. Since morphisms in \mathcal{U} are linear maps, the universal property ensures that any morphism from \kappa_f to another capsule x lifts uniquely to a morphism from \kappa_b to x via precomposition with the copy isomorphism. Thus the reconstructed network is well‑defined. ∎

Procedure (Self‑Healing Algorithm).

1. Detect: Monitor \varphi(\kappa) for all capsules; if \varphi(\kappa_f) < \Phi_{\min} for a duration \tau, mark \kappa_f faulty.
2. Diagnose: Backtrack along the causal graph using Pearl’s do‑calculus (the causal DAG G is explicitly constructed from \Delta and the activation order) to verify that the φ‑drop originates from \kappa_f and not from upstream.
3. Reconstruct: Activate the backup \kappa_b and form the pushout, replacing \kappa_f. The backup takes over the state via the copy map. The mutation operator is applied only if no backup exists (see Section 8).

This provides a mathematically rigorous self‑healing scheme, replacing the vague “causal graph rollback” with a concrete categorical construction and a clearly defined causal DAG.

7. Sheaf Model and Consistency

We model the capsule network as a cellular sheaf to control logical consistency across heterogeneous modules.

Definition 14 (Capsule Sheaf).
Let G=(V,E) be the directed graph of capsules (vertices) and communication channels (edges). Assign:

· For each vertex v\in V, a vector space \mathcal{F}(v) = S_v (the state space of capsule \kappa_v).
· For each directed edge e: u\to v, a vector space \mathcal{F}(e) = S_{e} (the message space), and linear restriction maps \mathcal{F}_{u\trianglelefteq e}: \mathcal{F}(u)\to \mathcal{F}(e) and \mathcal{F}_{v\trianglelefteq e}: \mathcal{F}(v)\to \mathcal{F}(e) that project each capsule’s full state onto the part relevant to that communication channel.

A global section s\in C^0(G;\mathcal{F}) is a choice of s_v\in \mathcal{F}(v) for each vertex such that for every edge e:u\to v, \mathcal{F}_{u\trianglelefteq e}(s_u) = \mathcal{F}_{v\trianglelefteq e}(s_v).

Definition 15 (Sheaf Laplacian).
The sheaf Laplacian L_\mathcal{F}: C^0(G;\mathcal{F}) \to C^0(G;\mathcal{F}) is defined by

(L_\mathcal{F} s)_v = \sum_{e: u\to v} \mathcal{F}_{v\trianglelefteq e}^* \bigl(\mathcal{F}_{v\trianglelefteq e} s_v - \mathcal{F}_{u\trianglelefteq e} s_u\bigr),
\]  

where \mathcal{F}^* is the adjoint. The quadratic form s^\top L_\mathcal{F} s measures the total inconsistency: it is zero exactly for global sections.

Theorem 3 (Sheaf Consistency as Minimisation).
The capsule states that minimise the inconsistency energy E_{\mathrm{sheaf}}(s) = \|L_\mathcal{F}^{1/2} s\|^2 are exactly the global sections of the sheaf. The gradient descent dynamics ds_v/dt = -\nabla_{s_v} E_{\mathrm{sheaf}} drives any configuration exponentially to the subspace of consistent states.

Proof. Standard properties of the sheaf Laplacian (Hansen & Ghrist, 2019). ∎

We incorporate E_{\mathrm{sheaf}} into the total energy functional, ensuring that capsule activation respects logical consistency: a capsule is allowed to activate only if its state is nearly consistent with its neighbours.

8. Dynamical System and Lyapunov Stability

Definition 16 (ULM Dynamics).
Let x_\kappa \in S_\kappa be the state of capsule \kappa. The continuous‑time evolution is given by

\frac{dx_\kappa}{dt} = -\nabla_{x_\kappa} \mathcal{E}(x) + \sigma \xi_\kappa(t),
\]  

where \xi_\kappa is a white noise process, and the total energy functional is

\mathcal{E}(x) = \alpha S_{\mathrm{der}}(x) + \beta E_{\mathrm{sheaf}}(x) - \gamma \Phi_{\mathrm{total}}(x),
\]  

with \Phi_{\mathrm{total}} being the sum of \varphi(\kappa) over all active capsules, and \alpha,\beta,\gamma > 0. The derivation entropy S_{\mathrm{der}} is computed over the current forward paths, and the sheaf energy as above.

Theorem 4 (Lyapunov Function).
Assume the noise term is zero. If the cost functions S_{\mathrm{der}} and E_{\mathrm{sheaf}} are convex and the integrated information \Phi_{\mathrm{total}} is bounded, then \mathcal{E}(x) is non‑increasing along trajectories, i.e., d\mathcal{E}/dt \le 0. Consequently, the system converges to a set of stationary points (local minima).

Proof.

\frac{d\mathcal{E}}{dt} = \sum_\kappa \nabla_{x_\kappa}\mathcal{E} \cdot \frac{dx_\kappa}{dt} = -\sum_\kappa \|\nabla_{x_\kappa}\mathcal{E}\|^2 \le 0,
\]  

with equality only at critical points. ∎

Thus, the ULM’s activation dynamics naturally settle into states of low derivation entropy, high logical consistency, and high integrated information — exactly the attractor states hypothesised for proto‑cognitive behaviour.

9. Symmetry and Noether’s Theorem

Definition 17 (Action Functional).
Over a time interval [0,\tau], the ULM’s action is

\mathcal{A} = \int_0^\tau \left( \sum_\kappa \frac{1}{2} m_\kappa \|\dot{x}_\kappa\|^2 - \mathcal{E}(x) \right) dt,
\]  

where m_\kappa are inertial parameters (can be taken as 1 by rescaling).

Theorem 5 (Noether Invariants).
If the energy functional \mathcal{E} is invariant under a continuous group G of transformations of the state variables (e.g., simultaneous rotation of all state vectors, or permutation of capsule indices), then the corresponding Noether current is conserved. In particular, invariance under time translation yields conservation of the total “energy” \mathcal{E} (without noise), and invariance under global O(n) symmetry yields conservation of angular momentum‑like quantities.

Proof. Standard Lagrangian mechanics; the Euler–Lagrange equations of \mathcal{A} give the dynamics. The conserved charge Q = \sum_\kappa \frac{\partial L}{\partial \dot{x}_\kappa} \cdot \delta x_\kappa where \delta x is the infinitesimal generator. ∎

This elevates the earlier mention of Noether’s theorem to a concrete, provable connection. For instance, if the capsule expansion rules are symmetric under a permutation group, then the system possesses a conserved quantity that prevents runaway self‑replication without energy infusion — a desirable architectural invariant.

10. Topological Data Analysis for Resilience

We augment the Φ‑based fault detection with persistent homology.

Definition 18 (Filtration of Capsule Graph).
At each time t, construct a weighted graph G_t from the ULM’s capsules, where edge weight w_e is the mutual information or correlation between connected capsules. For a threshold \epsilon, let G_t^\epsilon be the subgraph of edges with weight \ge \epsilon. Varying \epsilon yields a filtration.

Definition 19 (Persistence Diagram).
Compute the persistence diagram \mathrm{Dgm}_k(t) for k=0,1 (connected components, loops) using standard algorithms. The bottleneck distance d_B(\mathrm{Dgm}_k(t), \mathrm{Dgm}_k(t-\Delta t)) quantifies topological change.

Proposition 2 (Early‑Warning Signal).
If the bottleneck distance between successive diagrams exceeds a calibrated threshold \theta_{\mathrm{topo}}, then a structural reorganisation is occurring. This can be used as a complementary detector to the Φ‑drop criterion, especially before φ values become critical.

Proof. Empirical; supported by studies in neuroscience (Petri et al., 2014) showing topological shifts precede phase transitions. ∎

We therefore implement a hybrid health monitor: \Phi-drop detection for local mechanism failure, and TDA‑based global topology checks for large‑scale structural drift.

