A.6 Dynamical Systems and Lyapunov Stability

Definition A.18 (Autonomous ODE).
A dynamical system on \mathbb{R}^m is given by \dot{x}=f(x). A point x^* is an equilibrium if f(x^*)=0.

Definition A.19 (Lyapunov Function).
A continuously differentiable function V:\mathbb{R}^m\to\mathbb{R} is a Lyapunov function for \dot{x}=f(x) if V(x)\ge 0, V(x)=0 only at equilibria, and \dot{V}(x)=\nabla V(x)\cdot f(x)\le 0 for all x.

Theorem A.2 (Lyapunov Stability).
If a Lyapunov function exists, then every trajectory converges to the set of equilibria.

Proof. Standard (Khalil, 2002). ∎

