A.7 Symmetry and Noether’s Theorem

Theorem A.3 (Noether’s Theorem – Lagrangian Mechanics).
Let the action \mathcal{A}=\int L(q,\dot{q})dt be invariant under an infinitesimal transformation \delta q. Then the quantity

Q = \frac{\partial L}{\partial \dot{q}}\cdot \delta q

is conserved along solutions of the Euler–Lagrange equations.

Proof. See Goldstein (2002). ∎

